body:
@belchevgb , I am not quite understand your reproduce logic, 

```
ngAfterViewInit(): void {
    this.timeoutId = setTimeout(() => {
      // do some work
    });
  }

  ngOnDestroy(): void {
    clearTimeout(this.timeoutId);
  }
```

the `setTimeout` in `ngAfterViewInit` has been invoked after `0ms`, and in `ngDestroy`, `clearTimeout` will do nothing since the timeout is already done.

So could you create reproduce repo to show the issue?

@belchevgb , BTW, even after this memory leak issue is fixed, the test case you wrote may still have issues.


1. After the issue is fixed, in your code, You create a `setTimeout` inside a `it()` with a `fakeAsync()`, and `clearTimeout()` inside a `afterEach()`.

```
afterEach(() => {
    fixture.destroy();
    fixture = null;
  });

  it("test 1", fakeAsync(() => {
    fixture.detectChanges();
    tick();
  }));
```

So even without memory leak, the `fixture.destroy() -> ngOnDestroy() -> clearTimeout()` will not really clear the timer since 
they are not in the same `it()` or `afterEach()` testBody, it will not become a issue in this case (there will be no memory leak in this case) but it may become an issue for more complex case, so you need to call `fixture.destroy()` in the `it()` test body.

```
 it("test 1", fakeAsync(() => {
    fixture.detectChanges();
    tick();
    fixture.destroy();
  }));
```

I understand it is bolierplate code, so you may write some high order function like

```
function fakeAsyncWithAutoDestroy(testName, testFunc) {
  return it(testName, fakeAsync(() => {
    testFunc();
    fixture.destroy();
  });
}
itWithAutoDestroy('test', () => {
   ...
});
```

2. In your sample code, if your `leaky.component.ts` `ngAfterViewInit` code, if you give a delay of the `setTimeout`, 
```
    this.timeoutId = setTimeout(() => {
      // do some work
    }, 200);
```  
Then in your test code

```
 it("test 1", fakeAsync(() => {
    fixture.detectChanges();
    tick();
  }));
```

It will report `pending timer still remains in fakeAsync()`, since the timeout is not consumed or cleared.
